  "notes": "Cause code is TBD/provisional per FORM-366 fields; narrative states a causal investigation is scheduled and a supplement will follow. Duration reported as 36 months, 3 days, 1 hour, 16 minutes from 11/01/2021 to 11/05/2024 in Section III.B, though the timeline in Section E shows PCV-0656A declared OPERABLE on 11/04/2024 (1254 CST) after being declared inoperable on 10/05/2024; the extended inoperability period referenced spans back to a 2021 event per the TS 3.0.4/3.4.4 background discussion. Numerous other transient dual-PORV-inoperable events (battery bank, QDPS APC D1, block valve maintenance) are noted in the timeline as context for repeated TS 3.0.4 non-compliance but are not modeled as separate FailureModes since they are background/historical narrative rather than the reportable failure chain itself. PCV-0655A and its block valve are mentioned as contextual/parallel PORV train components, not part of the failure chain for this event's component failure (loose wiring in PCV-0656A)."
